<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Front end clues to back end issues on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/3-investigate/</link><description>Recent content in Front end clues to back end issues on Splunk Observability Cloud Workshops</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/3-investigate/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Funnel Dropoff</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/3-investigate/1-dropoff/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/3-investigate/1-dropoff/</guid><description>&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Examine the funnel&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the Homepage to Order Confirmation funnel, make sure the chart is showing &amp;ldquo;All users&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs" data-tabs&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs__list" role="tablist"&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-1-dropoff-md-1-1--0-tab-0" class="tabs__btn is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-1-dropoff-md-1-1--0-panel-0" tabindex="0" data-tab-label="Questions"&gt;Questions&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-1-dropoff-md-1-1--0-tab-1" class="tabs__btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-1-dropoff-md-1-1--0-panel-1" tabindex="-1" data-tab-label="Answers"&gt;Answers&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-1-dropoff-md-1-1--0-panel-0" class="tabs__panel is-active" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-1-dropoff-md-1-1--0-tab-0" data-tab-label="Questions"&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Which segment should we investigate?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click the segment and watch the replay. Pause, click different events, and scrub through as needed. What happened for the end user?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-1-dropoff-md-1-1--0-panel-1" class="tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-1-dropoff-md-1-1--0-tab-1" hidden data-tab-label="Answers"&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The last dropoff segment captures users who did not get from &amp;ldquo;Place order&amp;rdquo; to &amp;ldquo;Order confirmation&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In many cases for this app, the user is trying to place an order but getting an error message with a phone number to call after submitting the form.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So we see our users are trying to place orders but failing. Now what?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Follow the breadcrumbs</title><link>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/3-investigate/2-cause/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://splunk.github.io/observability-workshop/en/conf/2-user-journeys/3-investigate/2-cause/</guid><description>&lt;section class="exercise"&gt;
&lt;header class="exercise__bar"&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-icon" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/&gt;&lt;circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-label"&gt;Exercise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-divider" aria-hidden="true"&gt;·&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="exercise__bar-title"&gt;Investigate with RUM&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__panel"&gt;
&lt;div class="exercise__body"&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a user session with the order confirmation error message, click &lt;button class="btn-inline" type="button"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Troubleshoot in RUM&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt; in the top right of the replay. You should land on the long &lt;strong&gt;PlaceOrder&lt;/strong&gt; custom event in the RUM user session details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;figure class="figure"&gt;
 &lt;div class="figure__inner"&gt;
 &lt;img src="../images/rum-waterfall-place-order.png" alt="RUM session waterfall with PlaceOrder and APM link" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;
 &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs" data-tabs&gt;
&lt;div class="tabs__list" role="tablist"&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-2-cause-md-1-1--1-tab-0" class="tabs__btn is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-2-cause-md-1-1--1-panel-0" tabindex="0" data-tab-label="Questions"&gt;Questions&lt;/button&gt;&lt;button id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-2-cause-md-1-1--1-tab-1" class="tabs__btn" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-2-cause-md-1-1--1-panel-1" tabindex="-1" data-tab-label="Answers"&gt;Answers&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-2-cause-md-1-1--1-panel-0" class="tabs__panel is-active" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-2-cause-md-1-1--1-tab-0" data-tab-label="Questions"&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What is a likely cause of the Order Confirmation issue? How can you tell?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If you wanted to investigate this issue further, what would you do?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-2-cause-md-1-1--1-panel-1" class="tabs__panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tabs---home-runner-work-observability-workshop-observability-workshop-content-en-conf-2-user-journeys-3-investigate-2-cause-md-1-1--1-tab-1" hidden data-tab-label="Answers"&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The nearby POST request to the backend API is quite long, and throws a 500 error.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Because we&amp;rsquo;ve instrumented this app with both RUM and APM, we get related content between relevant requests. Hovering over the APM link on the long POST request, we see a likely root cause issue flagged on the payment service. So from here we could open the Place Order business operation in APM to see how widespread this issue is, and we can open the specific trace to see span details and any related logs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Walkthrough:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>